<!--5-->
<para>For questions 5 – 9, use the following information.</para>
<blockquote>The path of a toy rocket after launch is modeled by the following data set. The height of the rocket, in feet, \(y\), corresponds to the number of seconds passed, \(x\).</blockquote>
<div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-bottom="-10" data-left="-2" data-right="7" data-schema-version="1.0" data-tables="[[{&quot;variable&quot;: &quot;x_1&quot;, &quot;values&quot;: [0.4, 1,1.5,2.3,3.5]}, {&quot;variable&quot;: &quot;y_1&quot;, &quot;values&quot;: [20,41,52,60,52]}]]" data-top="70"/>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="4731440d-a3f0-41aa-8922-7dce76b457a1" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <para>What is the equation for the curve of best fit that models the data?</para>
  <exercise data-content-id="b90b03f7-6d4e-43e9-ab11-78fd7d4711c5" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(y = -9.2x^2+ 46x + 3.51\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(y = -6.1x^2+ 31x + 1.24\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y = -11.9x^2+ 30.2x + 3.64\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y = -4.2x^2 + 34x + 6.34\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(y = -9.2x^2+ 46x + 3.51\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>What is the equation for the curve of best fit that models the flight of the toy rocket?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.12.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="147dbf86-c93a-48c1-ab7f-05529b149e93" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="58.71 feet" data-solution-options="[&quot;45.91 feet &quot;, &quot;53.60 feet&quot;, &quot;58.71 feet&quot;, &quot;61.00 feet&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Approximately how high will the rocket be 2 seconds after launch?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 8.12.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="436af224-3161-411e-8ab5-eb1def5c2205" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="0.39 seconds after launch and 4.61 seconds after launch" data-solution-options="[&quot;0.26 seconds after launch and 4.74 seconds after launch &quot;, &quot;0.39 seconds after launch and 4.61 seconds after launch&quot;, &quot;0.52 seconds after launch and 4.48 seconds after launch&quot;, &quot;0.82 seconds after launch and 4.18 seconds after launch&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>At what approximate times after launch will the rocket have a height of 20 feet?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 8.12.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--8-->
  <exercise data-content-id="16d27a20-3e37-4123-b6d5-1fadbc84bd28" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="2.50 seconds" data-solution-options="[&quot;1.73 seconds&quot;, &quot;2.50 seconds&quot;, &quot;3.20 seconds&quot;, &quot;5.08 seconds&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Approximately how long will it take the rocket to reach its maximum height?</para>
